From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 17:32:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/10] .19 Execution Safety: required-vs-optional symbol
 handling for full coin universe

Same pattern as .13-.18: REQUIRED_SYMBOLS (BTC/ETH) remain the only
symbols whose missing/invalid reconciliation state can block the whole
safety report. Every other symbol .18 reports gets its own verdict
independently.

execution_authorized / paper_execution_authorized / live_execution_authorized
stay hard-coded False in every branch, for every symbol, unchanged by this
commit -- this file remains a non-authorizing, research-only report layer.
The required-vs-optional split only changes which symbol's bad data can
block the report; it does not touch, weaken, or bypass that boundary.

Specific changes:
- New reconciliation_state_errors_for_symbol() helper factors out the
  original per-symbol structural check (valid reconciliation_state, kept
  as the exact original allowed set -- flagged a pre-existing gap where
  v0.5.3.18's own UNVERIFIED state isn't in that set, left unchanged as
  out of scope here). verify_reconciliation()'s per-symbol loop scoped to
  REQUIRED_SYMBOLS only.
- build_safety()'s main loop iterates every symbol .18 reported (union
  with REQUIRED_SYMBOLS): required symbols keep the original verdict
  logic unchanged; optional symbols get the same verdict logic plus their
  own structural check, with a BLOCKED verdict (conflict, blocked, or
  invalid data) recorded in optional_symbols_blocked without adding to
  the global blocked_reasons or affecting the required pair. An active
  kill switch still blocks every symbol via the single existing global
  KILL_SWITCH_ACTIVE reason, without redundantly listing every optional
  symbol too.
- print_report() iterates actual decisions instead of a fixed BTC/ETH
  tuple, labeling each symbol REQUIRED/OPTIONAL.

Adds 9 contract tests, all of which explicitly assert
execution_authorized/paper_execution_authorized/live_execution_authorized
stay False across every scenario (kill switch on/off, clean/conflicted/
invalid required and optional symbols). Full suite (79 tests) green.

